# tools/inter_byte_matrix.sh — the INTER campaign's 96-cell frontier
#
# grid    {uniform,gradient,diag,screen} x {16,64,72,128} x {q20,q40,q55}
#         x {p6,p8}, frames=2 low-delay P, SVTAV1_FRAME_SHIFT=3
# host    Apple M4 Pro, aarch64-apple-darwin
# date    2026-09-02
# after   docs/INTER-ENCODE-PLAN.md §1z⁹ (PD0 inter compensation + the inter MD
#         lambda's rdmult base) and §1z¹⁰ (PD0's rate tables from
#         md_frame_context)
#
#   BOTH   31 -> 36      F1DIFF 64 -> 59      F0DIFF 1 -> 1
#
# CLOSED by §1z⁹, all five on the p8 arm where PD0 decides the whole tree:
#   gradient 64x64  q20 p8      gradient 72x72 q20 p8
#   diag     64x64  q20 p8      diag     64x64 q40 p8   (the reference cell)
#   screen   16x16  q20 p8
#
# §1z¹⁰'s rate-table fix is VERDICT-NEUTRAL on this grid — it moved seven
# F1DIFF cells' frame-1 byte counts (both up and down, none crossing) and
# closed none. It landed because it makes the port's PD0 block cost join C's
# `SVT_PD0COST_OUT` field for field on the reference cell (dist / ybits / cost
# / lambda all equal), which is the oracle the next chunk reads.
#
# STILL OPEN, in the order the dumps rank them:
#   1. `depth_removal_ctrls` is unwired in PD0. C resolves dr=1/0/1/1 on the
#      reference cell (disallow_below_32x32 AND _16x16) where Pd0Ctx::min_sq is
#      a flat 8. Inert on the five closed cells because the i == 0 early exit
#      fires above it; it binds wherever the parent is not well enough
#      predicted for that exit.
#   2. `gradient 128x128 q20 p8` — the ONE F0DIFF cell, a video-KEY defect,
#      7453 B against C's 7472. Every frame-1 reading on that cell is void.
#
# Reproduce: tools/inter_byte_matrix.sh
# Assert:    tools/inter_byte_gate.sh (36 required cells + 3 named open)
